      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstdlib>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n,s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\n\t// Allocate aligned flat array for better SIMD alignment and cache locality\n\tint* matrix = nullptr;\n\tif (posix_memalign((void**)&matrix, 64, static_cast<size_t>(n) * n * sizeof(int)) != 0) {\n\t\treturn 1; // allocation failure\n\t}\n\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i*n + j]));\n\n\tassert(s<n);\n\tassert(n<8000);\n\tassert(s>0);\n\tassert(n>0);\n\n\tint sum = 0;\n\t// Collapse initial two loops to expose more parallelism and use aligned assumption\n\t#pragma omp simd collapse(2) reduction(+:sum)\n\tfor(int i=0;i<s;i++) {\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<s;j++)\n\t\t\tsum += matrix[i*n + j];\n\t}\n\n\tint mxSum = sum;\n\n\tint dir = 1;\n\tint i = 0;\n\tint j = 0;\n\twhile(i+s <= n) {\n\t\tif( (j+s == n && dir==1) || (j==0 && dir==-1) ) { \n\t\t\tint exitingRow = i;\n\t\t\tint enteringRow = exitingRow+s;\n\t\t\tif(enteringRow >=n) break;\n\n\t\t\t// Combine subtract and add into a single SIMD reduction loop to reduce overhead\n\t\t\t#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {\n\t\t\t\tsum -= matrix[exitingRow*n + (k+j)];\n\t\t\t\tsum += matrix[enteringRow*n + (k+j)];\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\ti++;\n\t\t\tdir*=-1;\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tint exitingCol,enteringCol;\n\t\t\tif(dir==1) {\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = j;\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = exitingCol + s;\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = j-1;\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = enteringCol + s;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Combine subtract and add into a single SIMD reduction loop for column updates\n\t\t\t#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {\n\t\t\t\tsum -= matrix[(k+i)*n + exitingCol];\n\t\t\t\tsum += matrix[(k+i)*n + enteringCol];\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tj+=dir;\n\t\t}\n\t\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\",mxSum);\n\n\tfree(matrix);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining subtract/add loops into single SIMD reduction per update step, using a flat aligned array with posix_memalign and __builtin_assume_aligned (via alignment clause) to improve vectorization, and collapsing the initial sum loop reduces loop overhead and enables better auto-vectorization on ARM64 while preserving correctness.",
  "notes": "Changed matrix storage from vector of vectors to flat aligned array for contiguous memory layout. Combined separate subtract and add loops into single reduction loops for both row and column updates. Added collapse(2) pragma on initial sum loop. These transformations aim to reduce loop overhead, improve cache locality, and enable better SIMD utilization by the compiler.",
